WHY THEY ARE CALLED "DANGLING"
buffers[0] ---> 0xA100 (freed)
buffers[1] ---> 0xB200 (freed)
buffers[2] ---> 0xC300 (freed)
Meaning:

The pointer still exists, but memory behind it is gone.

After free:

Undefined behavior:
- garbage data
- kernel crash
- memory corruption






